# Way — environment template
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values:  cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Secrets are SERVER-ONLY (no VITE_ prefix). They are read by the serverless
# functions in /api (and the Vite dev middleware) and are never inlined into the
# client bundle. Only the Supabase anon key + URL are exposed client-side, which
# is safe by design. In Vercel, add the server-only keys as "Sensitive".

# --- Supabase (client-safe) -------------------------------------------------
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- ElevenLabs (Rhema voice) — server-only, read by /api/tts ---------------
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# Per-language voices: Way is bilingual, so English uses a neutral-English voice
# and Korean a native-Korean one (a single voice always accents one language).
# EN = Sarah (neutral American); KO = Anna Kim (Korean-native, tender/calm).
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID_EN=EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID_KO=uyVNoMrnUku1dZyVEXwD
# Legacy single-voice fallback (used only if the per-language vars are unset).
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=uyVNoMrnUku1dZyVEXwD

# --- Scripture — server-only, read by /api/bible ----------------------------
# The personal library is English-only: /api/bible serves English via the
# Crossway ESV API (api.esv.org). The ESV API license forbids storing verse
# text, which matches our rule: never persist Scripture, always fetch live.
ESV_API_KEY=
# Korean (개역개정) has no licensed API source, so Korean personal lookups are not
# offered — Korean Scripture lives in the curated curriculum as verified seed
# text. API_BIBLE_KEY is unused unless a licensed Korean bible is ever wired up.
API_BIBLE_KEY=
